From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 20:41:31 +0200
Subject: ASoC: mediatek: common: Keep DAI link references until the card binds

mtk_soundcard_common_probe() calls clean_card_reference() unconditionally
once devm_snd_soc_register_card() returns, dropping the OF references
taken by parse_dai_link_info() and clearing codecs[].of_node.

That is only safe if the card actually bound. snd_soc_bind_card() queues
a card whose binding was deferred on unbind_card_list and reports success
back to the caller:

	if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER) {
		list_add(&card->list, &unbind_card_list);
		ret = 0;
	}

The machine driver thus returns 0, is never re-probed, and never parses
the DAI link info again. The DT-derived codec entry has meanwhile had its
of_node cleared, and its name was already NULL because
snd_soc_of_get_dai_link_codecs() replaced the static entry with a zeroed
one in which only of_node and dai_name are filled in. When a later
component registration retries the queued card from
snd_soc_add_component(), the bind fails for good with

  ASoC: Neither Component name/of_node are set for DL_SRC_BE

and no sound card is registered at all.

Reproduced on a Radxa NIO 12L (MT8395) with the MediaTek audio drivers
built as modules. mt8195_mt6359 is loaded before snd_sof_mt8195 has
registered the ADSP platform component that the card's AFE_SOF_* links
need, so the first bind is deferred and the references are dropped. The
queued card is then retried from snd_soc_add_component() while SOF is
still probing, and dies there. Whether this is hit at all comes down to
module load order, so the same kernel and config can work on one distro
and fail on another.

Only release the references once card->instantiated confirms that the
card is bound.

Fixes: bce93a162505 ("ASoC: mediatek: Add common machine soundcard driver probe mechanism")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-soundcard-driver.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-soundcard-driver.c b/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-soundcard-driver.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-soundcard-driver.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-soundcard-driver.c
@@ -325,7 +325,12 @@ int mtk_soundcard_common_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ret = devm_snd_soc_register_card(&pdev->dev, card);
 
-	if (!needs_legacy_probe)
+	/*
+	 * A card whose binding was deferred is queued for a later retry and
+	 * reported back as success. That retry reuses the DAI link info parsed
+	 * here, so only drop our references once the card is really bound.
+	 */
+	if (!needs_legacy_probe && card->instantiated)
 		clean_card_reference(card);
 
 	if (ret) {
